<h2 class="sp-e495">How to Care and Clean Your Furniture to Make It Last Long?</h2>
<p class="sp-e513">
There are a few key things that you need to consider to keep your home
furniture looking its best.
</p>
<ol class="sp-e514">
<li class="sp-e511">
First, dust your furniture regularly with a soft, clean cloth. You can
also use a vacuum with a soft brush attachment on a low setting to
remove any dust that's hard to reach.
</li>
<li class="sp-e512">
Next, once or twice a month, you will want to give your furniture a more
thorough cleaning. You can do this by mixing water and white vinegar
equally in a spray bottle and lightly misting it on the surface of your
furniture. Wipe it down with a clean, dry cloth afterward.
</li>
<li class="sp-e512">
To protect your furniture from scratches and everyday wear and tear,
consider investing in felt pads for the feet of chairs and tables. You
can find these at your nearest hardware store. Peel off the adhesive
backing and stick it to the bottoms of your furniture legs.
</li>
<li class="sp-e511">
You can also call for professional services to inspect your furniture
completely. This will help you maintain your
<strong class="sp-e506">house furniture</strong> effectively and reliably.
</li>
</ol>
